> expand (x+y+z)^3
  ucas: expand (x+y+z)^3
expand (x + y + z)^3
  = x^3 + 3x^2*y + 3x^2*z + 3x*y^2 + 6x*y*z + 3x*z^2 + y^3 + 3y^2*z + 3y*z^2 + z^3
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> factor x^4 - 1
factor x^4 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor x^6 - 1
factor x^6 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + x + 1)*(x^2 - x + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor 6x^2 - 5x - 6
factor 6x^2 - 5x - 6
  = (2x - 3)*(3x + 2)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor x^5 + x + 1
factor x^5 + x + 1
  = (x^2 + x + 1)*(x^3 - x^2 + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor x^4 + 1
factor x^4 + 1
  = x^4 + 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor x^30 - 1
factor x^30 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + x + 1)*(x^2 - x + 1)*(x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x + 1)*(x^4 - x^3 + x^2 - x + 1)*(x^8 - x^7 + x^5 - x^4 + x^3 - x + 1)*(x^8 + x^7 - x^5 - x^4 - x^3 + x + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor x^3 + y^3
factor x^3 + y^3
  = (x + y)*(x^2 - x*y + y^2)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor 4x^2 - 9y^2
factor 4x^2 - 9y^2
  = (2x + 3y)*(2x - 3y)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor x^2 y + x y^2
factor x^2*y + x*y^2
  = x*y*(x + y)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor 2x^3 + 4x^2 + 2x
factor 2x^3 + 4x^2 + 2x
  = 2x*(x + 1)^2
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> collect x^2 y + x y + x^2 + 3, x
collect x^2*y + x*y + x^2 + 3
  = (y + 1)*x^2 + x*y + 3
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> simplify (x^2-1)/(x-1)
  ucas: simplify (x^2-1)/(x-1)
simplify (x^2 - 1)/(x - 1)
  = x + 1
  holds where x - 1 != 0 (cancelled there)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> cancel (x^2 - y^2)/(x - y)
cancel (x^2 - y^2)/(x - y)
  = x + y
  holds where x - y != 0 (cancelled there)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> together 1/x + 1/(x+1)
together 1/x + 1/(x + 1)
  = (2x + 1)/(x*(x + 1))
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> together a/b + c/d
together a/b + c/d
  = (a*d + b*c)/(b*d)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> apart 1/(x^2-1)
apart 1/(x^2 - 1)
  = 1/(2(x - 1)) - 1/(2(x + 1))
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> apart (2x+3)/(x^3-x)
apart (2x + 3)/(x^3 - x)
  = 1/(2(x + 1)) - 3/x + 5/(2(x - 1))
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> apart (x^3+1)/(x^2+1)^2
