> integrate 1/(x^3+1)
∫ 1/(x^3 + 1) dx
  = log(abs(x + 1))/3 - log(x^2 - x + 1)/6 + atan((2x - 1)/sqrt(3))/sqrt(3) + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 400 points of [-10, 10] (max difference 1.3e-15)
> integrate (x+1)/(x^2+2x+5)
∫ (x + 1)/(x^2 + 2x + 5) dx
  = log(x^2 + 2x + 5)/2 + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [-10, 10] (max difference 0)
> integrate 1/(x^4+1)
∫ 1/(x^4 + 1) dx
  = sqrt(2)*log(x^2 + sqrt(2)*x + 1)/8 - sqrt(2)*log(x^2 - sqrt(2)*x + 1)/8 + sqrt(2)*atan(sqrt(2)*x - 1)/4 + sqrt(2)*atan(sqrt(2)*x + 1)/4 + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [-10, 10] (max difference 3.3e-16)
> integrate x^3/(x^2+1)^2
∫ x^3/(x^2 + 1)^2 dx
  = 1/(2(x^2 + 1)) + log(x^2 + 1)/2 + C
  method: partial fractions, Hermite reduction for the repeated factors
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [-10, 10] (max difference 1.1e-16)
> integrate 1/(x^2+1)^3
∫ 1/(x^2 + 1)^3 dx
  = (3x^3 + 5x)/(8(x^2 + 1)^2) + 3atan(x)/8 + C
  method: partial fractions, Hermite reduction for the repeated factors
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [-10, 10] (max difference 2.2e-16)
> integrate 1/(x^2-2)
∫ 1/(x^2 - 2) dx
  = log(abs((x - sqrt(2))/(x + sqrt(2))))/(2sqrt(2)) + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [-10, 10] (max difference 2.3e-13)
> integrate (x^5+1)/(x^2-1)^2
∫ (x^5 + 1)/(x^2 - 1)^2 dx
  = x^2/2 - 1/(2(x - 1)) + 5log(abs(x + 1))/4 + 3log(abs(x - 1))/4 + C
  method: partial fractions, Hermite reduction for the repeated factors
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 399 points of [-10, 10] (max difference 4.3e-13)
> integrate 1/(x^4-2)
∫ 1/(x^4 - 2) dx
  = sqrt(2)*log(abs((2x - 2sqrt(sqrt(2)))/(2x + 2sqrt(sqrt(2)))))/(8sqrt(sqrt(2))) - sqrt(2)*atan(x/sqrt(sqrt(2)))/(4sqrt(sqrt(2))) + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [-10, 10] (max difference 6.8e-14)
> integrate 1/(x^3-2)
∫ 1/(x^3 - 2) dx
  = 0.2099868416log(abs(x - 1.25992105)) - 0.1049934208log((x + 0.6299605249)^2 + 1.190550789) - 0.3637078787atan((x + 0.6299605249)/1.091123636) + C
  method: partial fractions; the denominator has irreducible factors of degree >= 3: their roots are numeric, so the coefficients are decimals
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [-10, 10] (max difference 5e-14)
> integrate 1/(x^4+1) from 0 to 1
∫ 1/(x^4 + 1) dx
  = sqrt(2)*log(x^2 + sqrt(2)*x + 1)/8 - sqrt(2)*log(x^2 - sqrt(2)*x + 1)/8 + sqrt(2)*atan(sqrt(2)*x - 1)/4 + sqrt(2)*atan(sqrt(2)*x + 1)/4 + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 1] (max difference 3.3e-16)
  from 0 to 1: F(1) - F(0) = 0.866972987339911
  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 0.866972987339917, estimated error 9.5e-15
  the two agree to 6.1e-15
