> integrate x*cos(x)^2
∫ x*cos(x)^2 dx
  = x^2/4 + x*sin(2x)/4 + cos(2x)/8 + C
  method: product to sum: x/2 + x*cos(2x)/2, then by parts
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [-10, 10] (max difference 1.8e-15)
