  x = 3 - y
  y is free (any value)
  (a family of solutions: 1 free unknown)
  check: substituted into every equation (free unknowns at two values): residual 0
> solve x + y = 1, x + y = 2
  ucas: solve x + y = 1, x + y = 2
solve x + y = 1, x + y = 2 for x, y
  no solution: the equations are inconsistent (rank 1, the augmented system has rank 2)
> solve x^2 + y^2 = 1, y = x
  ucas: solve x^2 + y^2 = 1, y = x
solve x^2 + y^2 = 1, y = x for x, y
  eliminating y: the resultant in x is 2x^2 - 1
  x = -sqrt(2)/2, y = -0.7071067812
  x = sqrt(2)/2, y = 0.7071067812
  check: 2 solutions substituted into both equations: residual 1.1e-16
> factor x^4 - 1
factor x^4 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> expand (x+1)^5
  ucas: expand (x+1)^5
expand (x + 1)^5
  = x^5 + 5x^4 + 10x^3 + 10x^2 + 5x + 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> simplify (x^2-1)/(x-1)
  ucas: simplify (x^2-1)/(x-1)
simplify (x^2 - 1)/(x - 1)
  = x + 1
  holds where x - 1 != 0 (cancelled there)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> partial fraction decomposition of 1/(x^2-1)
  ucas: apart 1/(x^2-1)
apart 1/(x^2 - 1)
  = 1/(2(x - 1)) - 1/(2(x + 1))
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> decompose 1/(x^2-4) into partial fractions
  ucas: apart 1/(x^2-4)
apart 1/(x^2 - 4)
  = 1/(4(x - 2)) - 1/(4(x + 2))
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> put 1/x + 1/(x+1) over a common denominator
  ucas: together 1/x + 1/(x+1)
together 1/x + 1/(x + 1)
  = (2x + 1)/(x*(x + 1))
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
